			"notes": "## Kill Clipper v1.11.5\n\n### Replays look like what you saw\n- **First-person hands:** replays now record every swing, the hand bob when you place crystals or blocks, and the attack cooldown that lowers your held item, then play them back exactly. This works for clips recorded with 1.11.5 or newer. Older clips keep the old, rougher swing.\n- **Spectator camera:** flying around while editing is smooth now. The camera moves every frame instead of 20 times a second, even while the replay is paused.\n- **Players blinking out:** if you use EntityCulling, it no longer hides players during replays. It was guessing too late when the camera jumped, so players disappeared in spectator view.\n- **Blocks popping in:** an export now waits until the world around the camera is drawn before it records the first frame."
		},
