			"notes": "# Kill Clipper v1.11.0\n\n## Smooth exports\n- The editor now exports frame by frame. Every frame of the video is rendered on its own, so the export is perfectly smooth even when the game runs below your recording FPS. A slow PC just takes a little longer to export.\n- Exports no longer depend on the recording buffer, so long edits and slow-mo can't run out of room.\n\n## Sound in exports\n- Exports now carry the sound from your original kill clip, the same sound you heard while playing (including your own hits and crystals). Slow-mo parts slow the sound down to match.\n- Clips recorded with v1.11.0 or newer line the sound up exactly. Older clips can be off by up to a second.\n- If the clip's video was deleted, the export is saved without sound and the editor says so.\n\n## Export loading bar\n- A green progress bar shows at the top of the screen while the clip exports. It is drawn after each frame is captured, so it never shows up in the video.\n\n## Your deaths stay out of kill clips\n- When you die (death screen, or a chat line saying you died or lost), any kills before it are saved right away, ending just before the death.\n- The next clip starts after your death, so the round you lost isn't in the clip even with a long before-kill time. At least 2 seconds before the kill are always kept."
		},
