			"notes": "# Kill Clipper v1.9.0\n\n## Replays look right\n- You now show up in spectator and third person on every server. A stand-in with your skin walks, swings, crouches, wears your armour and takes hits like any other player.\n- First person no longer jerks around. Knockback, crystal and anchor explosions, and server corrections used to push the replayed you between recorded ticks.\n- A replay that ends in your death no longer opens the death screen.\n\n## Spectator keyframes (like Replay Mod)\n- In spectator, fly the camera to a spot and press **K** (or **+Key**) to drop a keyframe.\n- Move to another time and spot and add another.\n- The camera glides on a smooth curve through all the keyframes, easing in at the first and out at the last.\n- Keyframes show as white marks on the camera track. **C** / **Set spot** moves the keyframe under the playhead to where the camera is now.\n\n## Share as a link\n- **Share... → Get a link** uploads the clip and copies a link.\n- Paste the link in Discord and the video plays right in the chat. No webhook needed.\n- Clips go to catbox.moe (free, no account). Anyone with the link can watch.\n- You can still pick a vertical 9:16 version.\n\n## Export\n- After an export the editor comes back and tells you the file name it saved in your clips folder. Click the message to open the folder.\n- If an export can't be saved, the editor tells you why (for example the buffer is too short, or recording is off)."
		},
