			"notes": "# Kill Clipper v1.8.0\n\n## Editor\n- The video now sits on top, with the timeline and controls underneath it like a normal video editor. Nothing covers the picture anymore.\n- Spectator camera:\n  - Fly with WASD, Space and Shift (Ctrl to go faster) while the editor is open.\n  - Turn it by dragging on the video. With the editor hidden (E), use the mouse.\n  - You can steer it while the replay plays, too. Press **C** or **Camera spot** to keep the spot.\n- Your own aim and movement play back smoothly. Before, it could stutter and look like your aim was jerking.\n- Keys changed so they don't clash with flying the camera:\n  - **P** plays / pauses.\n  - **X** splits.\n  - The keys list now starts hidden; press **H** or **Keys** to show it.\n\n## Joining servers\n- Joining servers is faster. Recording fight replays used to rewrite every incoming packet (thousands of chunks while joining). It now just copies them.\n\n## Other\n- Discord uploads of long clips drop to 60 or 30 fps so they stay sharp.\n- The 9:16 copy, trimming and Discord shrinking run at low priority, so they don't cost game fps.\n- An export that slow-mo would make longer than the buffer warns you before it starts.\n- Stats are saved in the background and can't be half-written by a crash.\n- Share temp files are cleaned up."
