			"notes": "# Kill Clipper v1.7.0\n\n## One editor for trimming and camera views\n- Pick a clip in the Clip Editor list and press **Edit**. The fight opens straight into the editor; you no longer need to press E first.\n- The editor now works like a normal video editor:\n  - **Clip track:** drag the yellow ends to trim, or press **In** / **Out** (I / O) to trim at the playhead. Export only renders the trimmed part, and the bar shows how long that will be.\n  - **Camera track:** the fight is split into parts. Click a part to pick it, then use **POV** (1st person, 3rd person, spectator), **Speed** and **Zoom** to change that part.\n  - **Split** (S) starts a new camera part at the playhead, and **Merge** (Delete) joins a part into the one before it.\n  - For a spectator part, press E to hide the editor, fly the camera with WASD, Space and Shift, then press **C** (or **Camera spot** in the editor) to save that spot.\n- Press **H** or the **Keys** button to show or hide a list of every editor key.\n- Clips without a fight replay (older or imported videos) still open the trim screen from the same **Edit** button.\n- Exported clips no longer show chat or the \"saving\" message."
